==English==

===Etymology===
First attested in 1705. From {{suffix|en|Acadia|n|t2=one that is}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈkeɪ.di.ən/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Akkadian.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈkeɪ.di.ən/|/əˈkeɪ.d͡ʒən/|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|Akkadian}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪdiən|s=4}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or pertaining to [[Acadia]], its people, or their language or culture. {{defdate|First attested in the early 19th century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
# {{lb|en|geology}} Of or pertaining to the Acadian [[epoch]].

====Usage notes====
* The second US pronunciation is a rarely used historical version that led to the word [[Cajun]].<ref name=WI3>{{R:MW3 1976}}</ref>

