===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A native of [[Acadia]] or their descendants who moved to Louisiana; a [[Cajun]]. {{defdate|First attested in the early 18th century.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|Canada}} A descendant of the settlers of the French colony of Acadia in current eastern Canada.  More specifically a speaker of Acadian French.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|rare}} {{ellipsis of|en|Acadian French|t=the form of French spoken in Acadia}}.
#: {{ux|en|In many places, '''Acadian''' has been supplanted by English and by Standard French.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} The [[Middle Cambrian]] epoch, lasting from 497 million years ago to 509 million years ago.
#: {{ux|en|The Burgess Shale contains fossils of very odd organisms that lived during the '''Acadian'''.}}

